From 626a56874c4fb3f9edfbe4ce1421f58dbfe02eea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zack <zack@futo.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:57:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(geocoder): integer straddle test in point-in-polygon

A vertex decodes to f32(base + k * scale), monotone in k, so the straddle test is an integer compare against the point threshold; only straddling edges decode. Same answers on 419,221 points x 2 sets, per-polygon and arc files.
---
 geocoder/server/src/lib.rs | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 70 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/geocoder/server/src/lib.rs b/geocoder/server/src/lib.rs
